ddressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHASHI ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAO, YOSHIHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OOHASHI, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAO YOSHIHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OOHASHI ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAO, YOSHIHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OOHASHI, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An alternating current generator for vehicles, which is directed to decreasing sound pressure of cooling air and enhancing a cooling effect, comprising a casing composed of a pair of facing brackets each having a bracket body provided with an exhaust port rib forming a plurality of exhaust ports, and a plurality of suction port ribs disposed inside the exhaust ports and forming a plurality of suction ports, wherein at least one of the brackets has its exhaust port rib inclined 20 DEG  to 50 DEG  in the direction of rotating of a rotor with respect to a radial line from a rotating shaft, and has a rib thickness of at most 50 % of the width of the exhaust ports on the normal surface in the direction of inclination of the exhaust port rib.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un générateur de courant alternatif pour véhicules, qui vise à réduire une pression sonore d'air de refroidissement et à améliorer un effet de refroidissement. Le générateur comporte un logement composé de deux supports face à face, chacun présentant un corps de support pourvu d'une arête d'orifices d'échappement formant plusieurs orifices d'échappement, et de plusieurs arêtes d'orifices d'aspiration placées dans les orifices d'échappement et formant plusieurs orifices d'aspiration. Au moins un des supports présente une arête d'orifices d'échappement inclinée de 20 DEG  à 50 DEG  dans le sens de rotation d'un rotor par rapport à une ligne radiale d'arbre rotatif, et une épaisseur d'arête atteignant au plus 50 % de la largeur des orifices d'échappement situés sur la surface normale dans le sens de l'inclinaison de l'arête d'orifices d'échappement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>